Falsifies `address_space_map::verification::check_image_places_exactly_what_the_image_band_holds`.

The defect: `Band::holds` treats the band's end as exclusive for `end` too, so an image that fills
the image band exactly is refused, and as outside the band rather than as too large.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert_eq!(check_image(start, end), expected)`, at `end = IMAGE.end`.

diff --git a/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs b/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs
index 0eba0def7..8895744a1 100644
--- a/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@ impl Band {
 
     /// Does the whole of `[start, end)` lie inside the band? An empty or inverted range does not.
     pub const fn holds(&self, start: u64, end: u64) -> bool {
-        start < end && start >= self.start && end <= self.end
+        start < end && start >= self.start && end < self.end
     }
 }
 
